From: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc3: dwc3-msm: skip extcon suppliers stuck in probe-defer

On the TicWatch Pro 5 (dace) the dwc3 glue's DT extcon property lists two
suppliers: the pm5100 charger (qpnp-smblite) and the EUD. The charger driver
belongs to the out-of-tree BMS techpack and is not shipped in our first-stage
module set, so its device never probes and extcon_get_edev_by_phandle()
returns -EPROBE_DEFER for it forever. dwc3_msm_extcon_register() propagates
the defer immediately, so the glue never finishes probing and no UDC is ever
registered -- USB/adb stays dead even though the EUD extcon (the one that
actually drives USB-attach events on this device) is available.

Skip suppliers that are still deferred, register with the ones that are
present, and only fall back to -EPROBE_DEFER when none succeeded. Behaviour
for fully-populated systems is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
Signed-off-by: Cristodcgomez <cristo.c.mc@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-msm-core.c
@@ -4688,7 +4688,8 @@
 	struct device_node *node = mdwc->dev->of_node;
 	struct extcon_dev *edev;
 	int idx, extcon_cnt, ret = 0;
-	bool check_vbus_state, check_id_state, phandle_found = false;
+	bool check_vbus_state, check_id_state, phandle_found = false,
+	     deferred = false;
 
 	extcon_cnt = of_count_phandle_with_args(node, "extcon", NULL);
 	if (extcon_cnt < 0) {
@@ -4703,8 +4704,18 @@
 
 	for (idx = 0; idx < extcon_cnt; idx++) {
 		edev = extcon_get_edev_by_phandle(mdwc->dev, idx);
-		if (IS_ERR(edev) && PTR_ERR(edev) != -ENODEV)
-			return PTR_ERR(edev);
+		if (IS_ERR(edev)) {
+			if (PTR_ERR(edev) == -EPROBE_DEFER) {
+				/* dace: a supplier (e.g. the pm5100 smblite charger)
+				 * may never probe when its module is not shipped;
+				 * proceed with the suppliers that did probe.
+				 */
+				deferred = true;
+				continue;
+			}
+			if (PTR_ERR(edev) != -ENODEV)
+				return PTR_ERR(edev);
+		}
 
 		if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(edev))
 			continue;
@@ -4740,6 +4751,8 @@
 	}
 
 	if (!phandle_found) {
+		if (deferred)
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 		dev_err(mdwc->dev, "no extcon device found\n");
 		return -ENODEV;
 	}
